From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:05:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: xhci-plat: let a resume quirk say the controller lost
 its state

A platform's resume quirk may find that the controller lost power in the
sleep and set its glue up again. xhci_resume() then has to start the
controller over instead of restoring a state the controller no longer
has. Take a positive return from the quirk for that, as the
hibernation restore's power_lost does. The existing quirks (rcar, rzg3e,
cdns3 and dwc3) return zero or a negative error.

Signed-off-by: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>
---
 drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c
index b82ed7dfdc..3df2451901 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c
@@ -650,11 +650,12 @@ static int xhci_plat_resume_common(struct device *dev, bool power_lost)
 		}
 	}
 
+	/* A positive result: the controller lost its state, which the quirk set up again. */
 	ret = xhci_priv_resume_quirk(hcd);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret < 0)
 		goto disable_clks;
 
-	ret = xhci_resume(xhci, power_lost || priv->power_lost, false);
+	ret = xhci_resume(xhci, power_lost || priv->power_lost || ret > 0, false);
 	if (ret)
 		goto disable_clks;
 
